swarren@convex.com (Steve Warren) writes:
>Wishing SPOILERS ahead:

>
>The first thing to wish for is a blessed luckstone.  Once you have the luck-
>stone, don't ever drop it, as it looses its blessing from being dropped.  Once
>you have the stone you should find a unicorn and throw gems at it.  Ten
>unidentified stones will give you +10 luck, which is the max you can get with
>unidentified stones.  There is a way to get 3 more points (total of 13) of
>luck, but I forgot how it is done.

First, wishing for a blessed luckstone first can be a bad idea.  If your
wand has 1 charge, you will have to find a scroll of charging somewhere.
Just use the first wish for 3 blessed scrolls of charging.  Sure, you might
not get all 3, but you will get 1 and that's all you need.  Having two extra
scrolls of charging isn't worth the risk you take.... besides, you might get
3 anyway.

Luckstones do not change cursed/uncursed/blessed status when dropped.  The
only thing you risk when dropping a luckstone is having luck time out when
you aren't carring it.

Normally, luck goes from -10 to 10.  If you have a luckstone in your
posession, it adds 3 to the above limit if uncursed or blessed and
subtracts 3 if cursed.

The unicorn's alignment also affects what happens when throwing gems
at it.

>I recommend gauntlets of dexterity, a helm of brilliance, speed boots, and a
>cloak of displacement.  I think my favorite is the displacement cloak.  That
>really makes an incredible difference in the number of hits that you take.

Assuming you aren't the hacker with everything, I would recommend against
all the above except speed boots.  Magic markers, rings of levitation,
teleport control, scrolls of genocide, etc. are all more helpful than
increasing stats.

If you are the hacker with everything, it makes more sense to save the
wand until you need something than to increase stats.

>wish for 3 blessed scrolls of charging.  Then, I use my last wish (usually
>there are three wishes) to get a piece of armor.  Then I use a scroll of
>recharging (which only gives you one more charge).  Then I wish for a second

No, if it was a blessed scroll of charging, you will have a wand with
maximum charges.  In the case of a wand of wishing, that number is 3.
